---
import Guide from "@layouts/Guide.astro";
import { FOR_SERVICES_NAV } from "@data/nav-sections";
const crumbs = [{ name: "Home", href: "/" }, { name: "For services", href: "/for-services" }, { name: "Become a verifier", href: "/for-services/become-a-verifier" }];
---
<Guide title="Evaluate becoming a verifier" metaTitle="Evaluate a Verifier Pilot | identity.org.au" description="A proposed path for services evaluating reusable verification: select a workflow, agree issuer trust, complete integration and assurance, then measure a controlled pilot." lede="Start with a real decision your service makes. Production onboarding is not available through this website." eyebrow="For services · proposed path" breadcrumbs={crumbs} sectionLabel="For services" sectionNav={FOR_SERVICES_NAV}>
  <div class="prose-service">
    <h2>Bring an existing workflow</h2>
    <p>Identify the eligibility check, current evidence, repeated verification, failure rate and support effort. Choose the narrowest useful claim. The initial proposal explores membership eligibility rather than financial KYC or universal marketplace identity gates.</p>
    <h2>Agree who you trust</h2>
    <p>Use the <a href="/for-services/issuer-policy">proposed issuer policy</a> to establish claim authority, validity, status and complaints. Do not accept an issuer merely because its signature verifies.</p>
    <h2>Evaluate the experience</h2>
    <p><a href="/for-services/demo">Try the demo</a> with two fictional services. Its outcomes are simulated. It provides no real credential issuance, network registration or verifier approval.</p>
    <h2>Complete the production and assurance gates</h2>
    <p>Agree an actual interface and supported deployment, then demonstrate authentication, fresh request binding, status, privacy, recovery and alternatives. Decide any applicable accreditation route separately. The discussion pack lists required evidence.</p>
    <h2>Measure before expanding</h2>
    <p>Compare a bounded pilot with your current process. Agree readiness, costs, roles and evaluation criteria before enrolling real users. Participation is voluntary and no partner commitments are made by these materials.</p>
    <p><a href="/for-services/pilot">Read the pilot proposal and contact route</a> · <a href="/pilot/discussion-pack.md" download>Download the discussion pack</a></p>
  </div>
</Guide>
